[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011904628","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121520#issuecomment-5011904628","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121520","id":5011904628,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKruYdA","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T15:56:16Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T15:56:16Z","body":"If your system Display Settings have the reference luminance equal to the maximum luminance and your brightness setting to 100%, this is \"equivalent\" to SDR, so HDR output will do nothing. I'd first check that.\n\nIf those are set correctly such that either the brightness is less than 100% or the reference luminance is less than the maximum luminance, it's possible this is a bug in Godot, so we'll need to look further into this... Would you mind posting a screenshot of what the unmodified demo project looks like when embedded in the editor (with the game toolbar) something like this:\n\n<img width=\"1417\" height=\"724\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dca0df1e-b816-4269-a69d-634e6dc35951\" />\n\nThanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011904628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5012820054","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121520#issuecomment-5012820054","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121520","id":5012820054,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKsmQVg","user":{"login":"PlanetaryTyler","id":102492645,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhvp5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102492645?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler","html_url":"https://github.com/PlanetaryTyler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PlanetaryTyler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T20:32:18Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T20:32:18Z","body":"Ah amazing, that seemed to fix it, I assumed it was just doing good SDR to HDR tonemapping, not that it was effectively tricking it into thinking its HDR is SDR with those settings. May be good to note within some of the HDR docs. Do you have thoughts on if this happens to wayland across the board, or KDE Plasma specific?\n\n<img width=\"1437\" height=\"841\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/31b087f4-3246-4c29-a78f-d72888b9dada\" />\n<img width=\"1454\" height=\"913\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e1ca4d09-d9a1-4dc0-b0d1-3ff71588f04e\" />\n<img width=\"1006\" height=\"608\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/408866f7-6572-453a-b12e-e15b3462902f\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5012820054/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5013073110","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121520#issuecomment-5013073110","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121520","id":5013073110,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKs1s1g","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T21:55:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T21:55:33Z","body":"Ah, good to hear that was the only problem.\n\nThe root cause is that Wayland has no API for apps like Godot to query whether it is in HDR or SDR mode, so when brightness is at 100% and the reference luminance matches the maximum luminance, Godot must assume that the Window is on a screen that is operating in SDR mode.\n\nYou're right, this is a documentation issue. If anyone is looking to fix this issue in the docs, maybe a note something a little like this could be added:\n\n> Godot does not support HDR output when the Wayland Display Setting's brightness is set to 100% and the HDR reference luminance equals the HDR maximum luminance. Simply reduce the brightness Display Setting to allow for HDR output in Godot.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5013073110/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]